From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 13:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: start the camera firmware at open
 by default

Applications open the camera a moment before they start streaming. On
T8132 the firmware boots afresh for every stream, and that boot sits in
front of the first frame. Starting it when the video node is opened
moves part of it into the gap the application leaves itself.

On a J604, a cold open with a 0.3 s gap between open and stream start
gave the first frame after 0.862, 0.856 and 0.863 s without this and
0.618, 0.617 and 0.617 s with it, and 20 open, stream and close rounds
in a row ran without a failed round or an error line. Start the
firmware at open by default; fw_prewarm=N gives the previous behaviour.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
index bd43dc571c..fef682f3c4 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
@@ -2298,12 +2298,12 @@ void apple_isp_fw_cool_work(struct work_struct *work)
  * Applications open the camera some time before they start a stream. With
  * fw_prewarm, an open starts the firmware in the background and leaves it
  * running as fw_keep_ms does (at least 10 s), so that the stream that
- * follows does not wait for the firmware start. Off by default.
+ * follows does not wait for the firmware start. On by default.
  */
-static bool fw_prewarm;
+static bool fw_prewarm = true;
 module_param(fw_prewarm, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fw_prewarm,
-		 "Start the camera firmware when the video node is opened (default: off)");
+		 "Start the camera firmware when the video node is opened (default: on)");
 
 void apple_isp_fw_prewarm_work(struct work_struct *work)
 {
